{
  "id": "vec-02-01",
  "slug": "adding-vectors",
  "title": "Adding Vectors: Tip to Tail",
  "courseId": "vectors-matrices",
  "chapterId": "ch2-vector-operations",
  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "To **add** vectors, add matching components:\n\n⟨a, b⟩ + ⟨c, d⟩ = ⟨a + c, b + d⟩.\n\nGeometrically, place the second vector's tail at the first's tip — the sum runs from the very start to the very end. This **tip-to-tail** picture is why forces and displacements combine the way they do.",
      "figure": "vec-tiptotail"
    },
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Adding is a journey: walk u, then walk v.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "vectorExplore",
        "mode": "add",
        "ux": 3,
        "uy": 4,
        "targetX": 7,
        "targetY": 1,
        "vxStart": 0,
        "vyStart": 0,
        "gridMax": 8,
        "prompt": "u = (3, 4) is fixed. Choose v so the journey u THEN v ends at (7, 1).",
        "successFeedback": "v = (4, −3). Watch the green arrow: v is drawn from the TIP of u, and the red arrow is the single hop that replaces both. Adding components is just bookkeeping for that journey.",
        "lowFeedback": "The trip ends at the wrong horizontal position. From 3, you need 4 more to reach 7.",
        "highFeedback": "The horizontal is right, but the height is wrong. From 4 you must come DOWN 3 to reach 1."
      },
      "cml": {
        "stage": "construct",
        "flagship": false,
        "kernel": "spatial-invariance",
