    {
      "id": "c2",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "**Subtraction** is adding the opposite: ⟨a, b⟩ − ⟨c, d⟩ = ⟨a − c, b − d⟩. Geometrically, u − v points **from the tip of v to the tip of u** — exactly the displacement idea (recall). Order matters: u − v and v − u are opposites.",
      "figure": "vec-subtraction"
    },
    {
      "id": "k2",
      "kind": "check",
      "body": "Subtract componentwise.",
      "conceptTag": "vec-add",
      "explanationVariants": [
        "⟨5, 3⟩ − ⟨2, 1⟩ = ⟨5 − 2, 3 − 1⟩ = ⟨3, 2⟩.",
        "Subtract each matching component: ⟨3, 2⟩."
      ],
      "widget": {
        "type": "mcq",
        "prompt": "Compute ⟨5, 3⟩ − ⟨2, 1⟩.",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "o1",
            "label": "⟨3, 2⟩",
            "correct": true,
            "feedback": "Right — ⟨5 − 2, 3 − 1⟩ = ⟨3, 2⟩."
          },
          {
            "id": "o2",
            "label": "⟨7, 4⟩",
            "feedback": "That ADDS. Subtraction: ⟨5 − 2, 3 − 1⟩ = ⟨3, 2⟩."
          },
          {
            "id": "o3",
            "label": "⟨−3, −2⟩",
            "feedback": "That's the reverse (⟨2,1⟩ − ⟨5,3⟩). The given order gives ⟨3, 2⟩."
          }
        ]
      },
